Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-16-2000||03:43 PM||||This is actually in my big 3/4ton van, but let's just say it's for my Fiero so some people don't get testy. Before, it took hours for the engine to heat up (for the temp guage to move) so I assumed thermostat. However, while driving today, the needle flew all the way to redline and beyond. So I shut off the car, turned it back on, and the needle went a bit higher. Did this a few times with the same results. Drove around like that for a while with the needle waaaay past the maximum notch on the temp guage. My question, shouldn't it have blown it's top or something? If it's not overheating (i'm going to say it's a thermostat) what could it be? Coolant sensor? But wouldn't that trigger a code? The actual guage? Doubting that... Thanks!||||reg||1
